        ],
        "text": "According to Leondra R. Kruger (Amicus Curiae for United States), according to Leondra R. Kruger (Amicus Curiae for United States), amicus counsel for the United States argues that affidavits may be permissible if the affiants are brought to court for questioning, highlighting a possible compromise between confrontation rights and procedural efficiency."
